ENTRY            20719   20190112   20190424   20190420       2273
SUBENT        20719001   20190112   20190424   20190420       2273
BIB                 13         31
TITLE      Level structure of 24Na observed in the total neutron
           cross section of sodium from 300 to 900 keV
AUTHOR     (S.Cierjacks, P.Forti, D.Kopsch, L.Kropp, J.Nebe)
INSTITUTE  (2GERKFK) Institut fuer Angewandte Kernphysik.
REFERENCE  (J,PL/B,29,417,1969) - first results
           (C,70HELSINKI,2,745,1970) - final results of res.param.
           (R,KFK-1000,(SUPP.2),1969) - part of Na total cr.sect.
REL-REF    (I,,S.Cierjacks+,J,RSI,39,1279,1968)
           (O,20157005,J.Nebe+,J,NP/A,185,113,1972) - final data
                                             for Ca res.param.
FACILITY   (ISOCY,2GERKFK)
INC-SOURCE .Neutrons were produced in bursts of 1ns duration by
            bombarding a uranium target with deuterons at a
            repetition rate of 19.13 Hz.
METHOD     (TOF) Flight path- 57m.
           .The incident beam was monitored by a gamma-pulse-
            shape discrimination detector placed at 6deg to the
            beam at a distance of 11m from the source.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Liquid scintillator (NE-213), 9cm in diam.
            and 1cm thick on an XP-1040 photomultiplier.
ANALYSIS   (MLA) Multilevel R-matrix description with a single
            open channel for elastic scattering.
MONITOR    .Transmission with target in/out cycle time 20min.
CORRECTION .For background and dead-time effects.
           .The combined corrections were typically a few pc of
            the open beam counting rate and did not exceed 20%
            below 1MeV.
HISTORY    (19770707C)
           (20190112A) SD:Updated to new date formats,lower case.
           ERR-ANALYS, STATUS, SAMPLE moved to Subent 002. REL-REF
           added.Ref.KFK-1069 moved to 20157.Subents 003-005 added
ENDBIB              31
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           34
ENDENTRY             1
